  "unresolved": [
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOUbWGks68r_ro",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 4716843677,
          "body": "<!-- devin-review-comment {\"id\": \"BUG_pr-review-job-d527c102bb6142dba8f11070458704fc_0001\", \"file_path\": \"bin/crush/lib/shell_screen.ml\", \"start_line\": 943, \"end_line\": 945, \"side\": \"RIGHT\", \"based_on_repo_rules\": false, \"kind\": \"bug\"} -->\n\n🟡 **Quoted search fallback forces approval**\n\n`parameter` treats literal `{@` in a quoted `find -name` fallback as a multiword expansion. The shell tool then requires explicit approval even though the pattern stays one argument.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Learn more</summary>\n\nThe shell tool’s [command dispatcher](https://github.com/gosuda/charamel/blob/38d586ae3b2bce634e854990844f1db0b7642618/bin/crush/lib/tools_shell.ml#L243-L252 \"bin/crush/lib/tools_shell.ml:243-252\") sends `Review` verdicts through explicit permission checks. For `find -name`, [exec_commands](https://github.com/gosuda/charamel/blob/38d586ae3b2bce634e854990844f1db0b7642618/bin/crush/lib/shell_screen.ml#L1628-L1630 \"bin/crush/lib/shell_screen.ml:1628-1630\") requests review when it cannot prove the pattern is a single argument. A quoted scalar parameter expansion stays one argument even when its fallback contains literal `{@`. The scanner mistakes that text for the start of `${@}`. In automatic-approval mode without a prompt or an explicit grant, [the permission check](https://github.com/gosuda/charamel/blob/38d586ae3b2bce634e854990844f1db0b7642618/bin/crush/lib/permission.ml#L140-L144 \"bin/crush/lib/permission.ml:140-144\") and [prompt handling](https://github.com/gosuda/charamel/blob/38d586ae3b2bce634e854990844f1db0b7642618/bin/crush/lib/permission.ml#L168-L175 \"bin/crush/lib/permission.ml:168-175\") then deny the search.\n\n**Example:** `find . -name \"${pattern:-{@*.txt}\" -print` passes `{@*.txt` as one pattern when `pattern` is unset, but the screen requires explicit approval.\n\n**Recommended fix:** Record the opening position of each parameter expansion in [dollar](https://github.com/gosuda/charamel/blob/38d586ae3b2bce634e854990844f1db0b7642618/bin/crush/lib/shell_screen.ml#L864-L869 \"bin/crush/lib/shell_screen.ml:864-869\"), and recognize a leading `@` only at that expansion’s parameter position. Apply the same position check to the `!prefix@` selector so literal fallback text cannot match that rule either. Keep the existing multiword verdict tests and add a Clear case for a quoted scalar fallback.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- devin-review-badge-begin -->\n<a href=\"https://app.devin.ai/review/gosuda/charamel/pull/32\" target=\"_blank\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-dark.svg?v=4\"><img src=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-light.svg?v=4\" alt=\"Devin Review\"></picture></a>\n<!-- devin-review-badge-end -->\n\n---\n*Was this helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to provide feedback.*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOUbWGks68r_sx",
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 4716843803,
          "body": "<!-- devin-review-comment {\"id\": \"ANALYSIS_pr-review-job-d527c102bb6142dba8f11070458704fc_0001\", \"file_path\": \"bin/crush/lib/shell_screen.ml\", \"start_line\": 1156, \"end_line\": 1156, \"side\": \"RIGHT\", \"kind\": \"analysis\"} -->\n\n🔍 **Wrong executable in env test**\n\nAfter `GROUP=value`, GNU `env` treats `-` as the executable. `env_command` skips it, so the test expects a refusal for an argument rather than the executable.\n\n<!-- devin-review-badge-begin -->\n<a href=\"https://app.devin.ai/review/gosuda/charamel/pull/32\" target=\"_blank\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-dark.svg?v=4\"><img src=\"https://static.devin.ai/assets/gh-devin-review-light.svg?v=4\" alt=\"Devin Review\"></picture></a>\n<!-- devin-review-badge-end -->\n\n---\n*Was this helpful? React with 👍 or 👎 to provide feedback.*"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
